{
  "version": 1,
  "what": "One row for each source that the audit may call or may never call. The gate sends nothing to a source that is not here or is not allowed. Each terms line and each robots.txt line is the host's own words, with its page and the date it was read. A key is named by its variable, never by its value.",
  "needs": {
    "ON1": "For each client domain: verify the domain in our own Search Console account (one DNS record at the client's domain).",
    "ON2": "For each client domain: add and verify the site in our Bing Webmaster account. One API key for our user.",
    "ON6": "The request for Business Profile API access (Google's contact form). It needs a profile that we manage, verified and active for 60 days or more.",
    "ON7": "For each client: the client makes our account a manager of its Business Profile.",
    "ON8": "The YouTube Data API turned on in our Cloud project, and one key.",
    "ON9": "BigQuery in sandbox mode on our Cloud project (no card)."
  },
